WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.533 --> 00:00:07.604
Gotta have a subsistence lifestyle
way to live out here.

00:00:07.604 --> 00:00:09.138
We eat from the sea. 

00:00:11.507 --> 00:00:12.775
From the birds.

00:00:15.378 --> 00:00:18.514
Not really other ways
to, uh, get food around here.

00:00:19.849 --> 00:00:24.654
Salmon only comes once a year and, uh,
gotta try and the time they come around.

00:00:39.135 --> 00:00:39.535
Argh.

00:00:40.937 --> 00:00:42.505
Come on fish.

00:00:46.843 --> 00:00:47.944
You see anything?

00:00:47.944 --> 00:00:49.245
No. Nothing.

00:00:50.847 --> 00:00:55.118
Absolutely nothing, Set our first net

00:00:56.853 --> 00:00:58.888
and we weren't catching anything.

00:00:59.322 --> 00:01:02.525
We’ll just keep going upriver
until we get the salmon.

00:01:05.428 --> 00:01:08.164
Pretty much a small window.

00:01:08.164 --> 00:01:09.866
Hopefully, we'll get some salmon.

00:01:15.571 --> 00:01:16.639
I see my boys,

00:01:16.639 --> 00:01:19.742
they’re gonna be another steppingstone
for our culture.

00:01:20.009 --> 00:01:24.147
That's all I am and that’s what I’m
passing down to my sons.

00:01:26.683 --> 00:01:28.284
It’s a little torn up.

00:01:30.119 --> 00:01:33.389
All right, you guys keep an eye on it.

00:01:33.756 --> 00:01:35.992
Gotta look around
when you’re coming up the bank.

00:01:35.992 --> 00:01:38.428
It might be from grizzlies, you know.

00:01:58.548 --> 00:02:01.918
This is your Grandma Christine’s cabin.

00:02:03.386 --> 00:02:04.987
Door is still locked.

00:02:08.224 --> 00:02:09.425
Holy cow.

00:02:11.994 --> 00:02:12.929
Damn.

00:02:14.931 --> 00:02:16.365
Squirrels came in.

00:02:17.934 --> 00:02:21.904
If it was a bear it would be demolished in here.

00:02:22.872 --> 00:02:25.675
start picking stuff up, grab a trash bag.

00:02:25.675 --> 00:02:27.777
We've been having some tough luck
all fall.

00:02:27.777 --> 00:02:29.779
We haven't really seen very many moose. 

00:02:30.813 --> 00:02:33.916
The story I was told
when I was a kid is everybody's got a bag

00:02:33.916 --> 00:02:35.351
that they carry around with them.

00:02:35.351 --> 00:02:37.186
And inside that bag is your luck.

00:02:37.787 --> 00:02:40.623
And all year, you’re supposed to work on
that luck and add to it.

00:02:40.623 --> 00:02:44.894
Put a little bit here and there.
Helping somebody out. Paying it forward.

00:02:47.096 --> 00:02:48.831
Little squirrel never hurt nobody.

00:02:55.605 --> 00:02:57.540
Well, let’s get this wood stacked up.

00:02:57.974 --> 00:03:02.245
The more we do, better chance
we will have.

00:03:04.947 --> 00:03:07.383
It is very important to me
to get better luck

00:03:07.917 --> 00:03:10.386
‘cause I love hunting
and I love seeing stuff.

00:03:10.386 --> 00:03:13.456
It just gives joy to me and
excitement.

00:03:15.258 --> 00:03:17.059
Already looking nicer, boys.

00:03:18.494 --> 00:03:20.897
We should play in that place.My
late brother

00:03:20.897 --> 00:03:24.801
came down by himself
and he built this little cache style

00:03:24.801 --> 00:03:25.701
house.

00:03:26.769 --> 00:03:29.338
It’s kinda like a little tree
house, the kids like it now.

00:03:30.239 --> 00:03:32.875
Yeah, that's
what my late brother made right there.

00:03:33.876 --> 00:03:35.678
This is called the boys club.

00:03:35.678 --> 00:03:37.446
No girls allowed.

00:03:43.986 --> 00:03:46.389
Boys come on! Let’s go.

00:03:46.389 --> 00:03:47.790
Get your life jacket.

00:03:48.724 --> 00:03:52.295
All right boys,
I feel a lot better about leaving camp.

00:03:52.895 --> 00:03:56.032
You know, we left it
a little better than what we found it.

00:03:56.199 --> 00:03:59.635
So, I feel like, you know,
we added some good luck to our bag.

00:03:59.802 --> 00:04:04.173
I feel, you know, we have a better chance
of seeing something out there now.

00:04:04.907 --> 00:04:07.944
Let's hope and pray
we see something on the way home boys.

